{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-78349" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the curve  $r(t)=t\\,i+\\sqrt{8}t\\,j-4t\\,k,$ $t\\ge 0,$ for which the arc length $s$ from $r(0)$ to $r(t)$ is given by $s=5t,$ find the corresponding unit tangent $T(s),$ parametrized by $s.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082537/state.json" "file_sha256" "313983a19d3388282dae223b56b6959610c9ae609d7ed7b24be7d05dff312a27"} {"question" "q-78349" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, since $s=5t$, we have that $t=\\frac{s}{5}.$  \n\nTherefore, the vector function $R(s)$ that parametrizes $r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\frac{s}{5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{s}{5}\\,i+(\\sqrt{8}\\cdot \\frac{s}{5})j-4\\cdot \\frac{s}{5}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{s}{5}\\,i+\\frac{\\sqrt{8}s}{5}\\,j-\\frac{4s}{5}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n   \n\nNow, since the curve is parametrized by its arc length $s$, the unit tangent can be found as\n\n$$\nT(s)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s).\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{s}{5})i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{\\sqrt{8}s}{5})j-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{4s}{5})k \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\,i+\\frac{\\sqrt{8}}{5}\\,j-\\frac{4}{5}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082537/state.json" "file_sha256" "313983a19d3388282dae223b56b6959610c9ae609d7ed7b24be7d05dff312a27"} {"question" "q-78349" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082537/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f464b2f967382051a79ecef4138be137187d04d717aa5c8f07a33d97c42c5c3d"} {"question" "q-78349" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082537/state.json" "file_sha256" "313983a19d3388282dae223b56b6959610c9ae609d7ed7b24be7d05dff312a27"} {"question" "q-78349" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{50}\\,i+\\frac{\\sqrt{8}}{5}\\,j-\\frac{4}{25}\\,k"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{5}\\,i+\\frac{\\sqrt{8}}{5}\\,j-\\frac{4}{5}\\,k"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{5}\\,i-\\frac{\\sqrt{8}}{5}\\,j-\\frac{2}{5}\\,k"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{5}\\,i+\\frac{\\sqrt{8}}{5}\\,j-\\frac{1}{5}\\,k"] ["math" "\\frac{s}{5}\\,i+\\frac{\\sqrt{8}}{5}\\,j+\\frac{4}{5}\\,k"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082537/state.json" "file_sha256" "313983a19d3388282dae223b56b6959610c9ae609d7ed7b24be7d05dff312a27"} {"question" "q-78349" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{5}\\,i+\\frac{\\sqrt{8}}{5}\\,j-\\frac{4}{5}\\,k"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082537/state.json" "file_sha256" "313983a19d3388282dae223b56b6959610c9ae609d7ed7b24be7d05dff312a27"} {"question" "q-127703" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the curve $r(t)=⟨{sin}^{2}⁡t,\\,{cos}^{2}⁡t,\\,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t⟩,$ $t\\ge 0,$ for which the arc length $s$ from $r(0)$ to $r(t)$ is given by $s=\\sqrt{2}\\,t,$ find the corresponding unit tangent $T(s),$ parametrized by $s.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082537/state.json" "file_sha256" "313983a19d3388282dae223b56b6959610c9ae609d7ed7b24be7d05dff312a27"} {"question" "q-127703" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, since $s=\\sqrt{2}\\,t,$ we have that $t=\\frac{s}{\\sqrt{2}}.$\n\nTherefore, the vector function $R(s)$ that parametrizes $r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\frac{s}{\\sqrt{2}}) \\\\  & =⟨{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{s}{\\sqrt{2}}),\\,{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{s}{\\sqrt{2}}),\\,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{s}{\\sqrt{2}})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{s}{\\sqrt{2}}),\\,{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{s}{\\sqrt{2}}),\\,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}\\,s)⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n   \n\nNow, since the curve is parametrized by its arc length $s$, the unit tangent can be found as\n\n$$\nT(s)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s).\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s) \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}({sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{s}{\\sqrt{2}})),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}({cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{s}{\\sqrt{2}})),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}\\,s))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{s}{\\sqrt{2}}),\\,-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{s}{\\sqrt{2}}),\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2}\\,s)⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}\\,s),\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}\\,s),\\,\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2}\\,s)⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082537/state.json" "file_sha256" "313983a19d3388282dae223b56b6959610c9ae609d7ed7b24be7d05dff312a27"} {"question" "q-127703" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082537/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f464b2f967382051a79ecef4138be137187d04d717aa5c8f07a33d97c42c5c3d"} {"question" "q-127703" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082537/state.json" "file_sha256" "313983a19d3388282dae223b56b6959610c9ae609d7ed7b24be7d05dff312a27"} {"question" "q-127703" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "T(s)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2s),\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2s),\\,\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})⟩"] ["math" "T(s)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}),\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}),\\,\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2s)⟩"] ["math" "T(s)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}\\,s),\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}\\,s),\\,\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{\\sqrt{2}})⟩"] ["math" "T(s)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}\\,s),\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}\\,s),\\,\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2}\\,s)⟩"] ["math" "T(s)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡s,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡s,\\,\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡s⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082537/state.json" "file_sha256" "313983a19d3388282dae223b56b6959610c9ae609d7ed7b24be7d05dff312a27"} {"question" "q-127703" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "T(s)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}\\,s),\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}\\,s),\\,\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2}\\,s)⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082537/state.json" "file_sha256" "313983a19d3388282dae223b56b6959610c9ae609d7ed7b24be7d05dff312a27"} {"question" "q-127709" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the curve $r(t)=⟨\\frac{3}{5}{t}^{3/2},\\,1,\\,\\frac{4}{5}{t}^{3/2}⟩,$ $t\\ge 0,$ for which the arc length $s$ from $r(0)$ to $r(t)$ is given by $s={t}^{3/2},$ find the corresponding unit tangent $T(s),$ parametrized by $s.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082537/state.json" "file_sha256" "313983a19d3388282dae223b56b6959610c9ae609d7ed7b24be7d05dff312a27"} {"question" "q-127709" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, since $s={t}^{3/2},$ we have that $t={s}^{2/3}.$ \n\nTherefore, the vector function $R(s)$ that parametrizes $r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r({s}^{2/3}) \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{3}{5}{({s}^{2/3})}^{3/2},\\,1,\\,\\frac{4}{5}{({s}^{2/3})}^{3/2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{3s}{5},\\,1,\\,\\frac{4s}{5}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n   \n\nNow, since the curve is parameterized by its arc length $s$, the unit tangent can be found as\n\n$$\nT(s)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s).\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s) \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{3s}{5}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(1),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{4s}{5})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{3}{5},\\,0,\\,\\frac{4}{5}⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}⟨3,0,4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082537/state.json" "file_sha256" "313983a19d3388282dae223b56b6959610c9ae609d7ed7b24be7d05dff312a27"} {"question" "q-127709" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082537/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f464b2f967382051a79ecef4138be137187d04d717aa5c8f07a33d97c42c5c3d"} {"question" "q-127709" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082537/state.json" "file_sha256" "313983a19d3388282dae223b56b6959610c9ae609d7ed7b24be7d05dff312a27"} {"question" "q-127709" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "T(s)=\\frac{1}{5}⟨3,0,4⟩"] ["math" "T(s)=\\frac{1}{5}⟨9,0,16⟩"] ["math" "T(s)=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}⟨\\sqrt{3},1,2⟩"] ["math" "T(s)=\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}⟨1,0,2⟩"] ["math" "T(s)=\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}⟨3,1,4⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082537/state.json" "file_sha256" "313983a19d3388282dae223b56b6959610c9ae609d7ed7b24be7d05dff312a27"} {"question" "q-127709" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "T(s)=\\frac{1}{5}⟨3,0,4⟩"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082537/state.json" "file_sha256" "313983a19d3388282dae223b56b6959610c9ae609d7ed7b24be7d05dff312a27"} {"question" "q-127732" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the parametrization of the curve $r(t)=⟨3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-2,\\,1-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,$ $t\\ge 0,$ by its arc length $s?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082537/state.json" "file_sha256" "313983a19d3388282dae223b56b6959610c9ae609d7ed7b24be7d05dff312a27"} {"question" "q-127732" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and its magnitude $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-2),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}^{2}+{(-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9{sin}^{2}⁡t+9{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the arc length of the curve from $0$ to $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}‖{r}^{′}(u)‖\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}3\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3u\\,{|}_{0}^{t} \\\\  & =3t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $s=3t,$ we have that $t=\\frac{s}{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the vector function that parametrizes $r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\frac{s}{3}) \\\\  & =⟨3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})-2,\\,1-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082537/state.json" "file_sha256" "313983a19d3388282dae223b56b6959610c9ae609d7ed7b24be7d05dff312a27"} {"question" "q-127732" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082537/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f464b2f967382051a79ecef4138be137187d04d717aa5c8f07a33d97c42c5c3d"} {"question" "q-127732" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082537/state.json" "file_sha256" "313983a19d3388282dae223b56b6959610c9ae609d7ed7b24be7d05dff312a27"} {"question" "q-127732" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "R(s)=-3⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{3}),\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})⟩"] ["math" "R(s)=\\frac{1}{2}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡2s,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡2s⟩"] ["math" "R(s)=⟨3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})-2,\\,1-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})⟩"] ["math" "R(s)=⟨3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{\\sqrt{3}})-2,\\,1-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{\\sqrt{3}})⟩"] ["math" "R(s)=⟨3\\operatorname{cos}⁡3s-2,\\,1-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡3s⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082537/state.json" "file_sha256" "313983a19d3388282dae223b56b6959610c9ae609d7ed7b24be7d05dff312a27"} {"question" "q-127732" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "R(s)=⟨3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})-2,\\,1-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082537/state.json" "file_sha256" "313983a19d3388282dae223b56b6959610c9ae609d7ed7b24be7d05dff312a27"} {"question" "q-127735" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the parametrization of the curve $r(t)=⟨1-{t}^{2},\\,2{t}^{2},\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}{t}^{2}⟩,$ $t\\ge 0,$ by its arc length $s?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082537/state.json" "file_sha256" "313983a19d3388282dae223b56b6959610c9ae609d7ed7b24be7d05dff312a27"} {"question" "q-127735" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and its magnitude $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-{t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}{t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2t,\\,4t,\\,\\sqrt{5}t⟩ \\\\  & =t⟨-2,\\,4,\\,\\sqrt{5}⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =|t|\\sqrt{{(-2)}^{2}+{(4)}^{2}+(\\sqrt{5})^{2}} \\\\  & =t\\sqrt{4+16+5} \\\\  & =t\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the arc length of the curve from $0$ to $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}‖{r}^{′}(u)‖\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}5u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =5{\\int }_{0}^{t}u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{u}^{2}\\,{|}_{0}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{t}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $s=\\frac{5}{2}{t}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{2}{t}^{2} & =s \\\\ {t}^{2} & =\\frac{2s}{5} \\\\ t & =\\sqrt{\\frac{2s}{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vector function that parametrizes $r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\sqrt{\\frac{2s}{5}}) \\\\  & =⟨1-{(\\sqrt{\\frac{2s}{5}})}^{2},\\,2{(\\sqrt{\\frac{2s}{5}})}^{2},\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}{(\\sqrt{\\frac{2s}{5}})}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1-\\frac{2s}{5},\\,\\frac{4s}{5},\\,\\frac{s\\sqrt{5}}{5}⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}⟨5-2s,\\,4s,\\,s\\sqrt{5}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082537/state.json" "file_sha256" "313983a19d3388282dae223b56b6959610c9ae609d7ed7b24be7d05dff312a27"} {"question" "q-127735" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082537/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f464b2f967382051a79ecef4138be137187d04d717aa5c8f07a33d97c42c5c3d"} {"question" "q-127735" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082537/state.json" "file_sha256" "313983a19d3388282dae223b56b6959610c9ae609d7ed7b24be7d05dff312a27"} {"question" "q-127735" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "R(s)=\\frac{1}{3}⟨1-s,\\,s\\sqrt{3},\\,s\\sqrt{5}⟩"] ["math" "R(s)=\\frac{1}{5}⟨1-3s,\\,4s,\\,s\\sqrt{5}⟩"] ["math" "R(s)=\\frac{1}{5}⟨5-2s,\\,4s,\\,s\\sqrt{5}⟩"] ["math" "R(s)=⟨1-{s}^{2},\\,2{s}^{2},\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}{s}^{2}⟩"] ["math" "R(s)=⟨{s}^{2}-1,\\,-2{s}^{2},\\,\\sqrt{5}{s}^{2}⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082537/state.json" "file_sha256" "313983a19d3388282dae223b56b6959610c9ae609d7ed7b24be7d05dff312a27"} {"question" "q-127735" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "R(s)=\\frac{1}{5}⟨5-2s,\\,4s,\\,s\\sqrt{5}⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082537/state.json" "file_sha256" "313983a19d3388282dae223b56b6959610c9ae609d7ed7b24be7d05dff312a27"}] "usage" {} "basis" 2859 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
